 <197308427+dangelrk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:10:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Answer yap -V before the argument-count check

"yap -V" is a complete invocation on its own, but the usage check ran
first and answered it with a usage message instead of the version.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/yap/c/yap.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/yap/c/yap.c b/src/yap/c/yap.c
index 697d20b..ef3872e 100644
--- a/src/yap/c/yap.c
+++ b/src/yap/c/yap.c
@@ -939,6 +939,16 @@ char **argv;
  char *eq;
  size_t n;
 
+ /* -V before the argument-count check: it is a complete invocation on
+ ** its own and must not be answered with a usage message. */
+ for (i = 1; i < argc; i++)
+     if (argv[i][0] == '-' && (argv[i][1] == 'V' || argv[i][1] == 'v'))
+     {
+	printf("yap %s build %s (%s)\n",
+	       YAP_VERSION,ACE_BUILD_NUMBER,ACE_BUILD_DATE);
+	exit(0);
+     }
+
  if (argc < 3) { show_usage(); return(FALSE); }
 
  for (i = 1; i < argc; i++)
